[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Building Cross-Platform Mobile Apps with NativeScript and Vue.js"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"NativeScript allows you to build native iOS and Android apps using JavaScript and popular frameworks like Vue.js. By combining NativeScript with Vue, you gain access to native device APIs and UI components while leveraging the reactive, component-driven architecture of Vue."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Prerequisites and Setup"},{"order":4,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Node.js installed on your development machine (LTS version recommended)."},{"order":5,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Android Studio and/or Xcode configured for native mobile builds."},{"order":6,"type":"bullet_point","text":"NativeScript CLI installed globally via npm install -g nativescript."},{"order":7,"type":"subheading","text":"Creating a New NativeScript-Vue Project"},{"order":8,"type":"paragraph","text":"To initialize a new project configured with NativeScript and Vue, run the following command in your terminal:"},{"order":9,"type":"code","text":"ns create my-vue-app --vue"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"Navigate into the newly created project directory to begin development."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"cd my-vue-app"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding the Project Structure"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"A standard NativeScript-Vue app contains an app directory where your components, assets, and main entry point reside. The app.js or main.js file initializes the Vue instance with NativeScript."},{"order":14,"type":"subheading","text":"Creating Your First Component"},{"order":15,"type":"paragraph","text":"Let us create a simple counter component using native UI elements like Page, ActionBar, Label, and Button. Open your app/components/Home.vue file and update it with the following code:"},{"order":16,"type":"code","text":"<template>
  <Page>
    <ActionBar title="NativeScript-Vue" />
    <GridLayout rows="auto, auto" class="p-20">
      <Label row="0" :text="message" class="text-center text-xl mb-20" />
      <Button row="1" text="Increment" @tap="increment" class="btn btn-primary" />
    </GridLayout>
  </Page>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  data() {
    return {
      counter: 0
    };
  },
  computed: {
    message() {
      return "Pressed " + this.counter + " times";
    }
  },
  methods: {
    increment() {
      this.counter++;
    }
  }
};
</script>"},{"order":17,"type":"subheading","text":"Running the Application"},{"order":18,"type":"paragraph","text":"You can run your application on an attached physical device or an emulator. Use the following commands to launch your app for Android or iOS:"},{"order":19,"type":"code","text":"ns run android
ns run ios"},{"order":20,"type":"paragraph","text":"Congratulations! You have successfully built and deployed a cross-platform mobile application using NativeScript and Vue.js."}]
